Ruling: Do not create or expand tests until the optimizer completes end to end — the user's current goal overrides plan steps that call for new test files; use existing focused tests, compile/lint checks, and direct deterministic smoke runs instead — cost if wrong: weaker early regression localization and more reliance on integration evidence.
Ruling: Execute the roadmap through nested detailed-plan ledgers rather than treating each multi-phase roadmap task as one oversized dispatch — preserves task-level review while following the same dependency order — cost if wrong: extra coordination overhead.

